[{:adr/authoritative_for ["ipns.head is a NEW NAMESPACE in the existing kotoba-lang/ipns repo (ADR-2607050100), not a new repo -- ipns.core (name derivation) already existed and stays zero-dep/portable; only ipns.head pulls in ed25519/dag-cbor" "ipns.core/pubkey->name is now cross-checked against a real Kubo 0.41.0 node's ipfs id / ipfs cid format output for the same Ed25519 key, in addition to the prior kekkai/kagi cross-check from ADR-2607050100" "kotobase.net resolves IPNS heads through its own XRPC registry (head.json/publish.json lexicon), not the real IPFS/libp2p DHT -- deliberate scope" "ipns.head/sign and verify are :clj-only (JCA Ed25519 via ed25519's did:key primitives, reused not reimplemented); :cljs porting for kotobase-client is a tracked follow-up" "addendum: kotoba-lang/ipns renamed to kotoba-lang/tech-ipfs-specs-ipns (reverse-domain external-spec convention, ADR-2607052300 precedent); dependents kekkai/kagi/tayori deps.edn coordinates updated (same pinned commit); manifest/repos.edn + west.yml updated, old west.yml entry removed manually (--entry doesn't auto-delete superseded entries)" "addendum 2: cljs/worker follow-ups closed same day -- kotoba-client's verify-ipns-head (JVM) resolves its NOT-implemented stub; kotobase-client gains kotobase.ipns/sign-head+verify-head (:cljs, own @noble/curves/@ipld/dag-cbor stack per ADR-2607050100 precedent, verified byte-identical to a real JVM-signed fixture -- payload AND deterministic signature both match); kotobase-cljc-worker wires com.etzhayyim.apps.kotoba.ipns.{head,publish} as a separate NSID family (unauthenticated self-verifying reads, signature-gated writes, sequence CAS via r2-get-head/r2-put-head-if-match); a lexicon/implementation mismatch was found (head.json's `graph` param has no graph-CID->IPNS-name derivation anywhere) and resolved by keying storage on the record's own :name field, owner-confirmed, fixing the lexicon itself left as a separate follow-up"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_b